From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:54:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [tests] Leave the D-Bus test out of the TSan run.

QtDBus does its socket work in its own thread inside the system Qt,
which is not built with TSan and passes data on under futex-based
QMutex that TSan cannot see, so TSan reports Qt copying the messages
handed to it. Suppressing that would take a pattern (memcpy, or any
frame in libQt5Core) that hides real races too. None of voicecall's code
runs on that thread, and the test still runs under ASan, UBSan and
valgrind.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tests/hardening/README |  3 +++
 tests/hardening/run    | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/hardening/README b/tests/hardening/README
index 5369126..aa91767 100644
--- a/tests/hardening/README
+++ b/tests/hardening/README
@@ -16,6 +16,9 @@ checker and runs every tst_* binary with:
   asan       AddressSanitizer + UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, any report
              is fatal, leaks included
   tsan       ThreadSanitizer, with ASLR off as TSan needs
+             (not tst_dbusservice: QtDBus does its work in a thread
+             of the uninstrumented system Qt, and TSan reports the
+             data that Qt hands over to it)
   valgrind   memcheck; fails on any error or definite leak
 
 Pass -c once per C++ compiler to build the sanitizer runs with (GCC and
diff --git a/tests/hardening/run b/tests/hardening/run
index 6ab058f..2ff0a38 100755
--- a/tests/hardening/run
+++ b/tests/hardening/run
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@ check() {
     } > "$log" 2>&1 || rc=1
     if [ $rc = 0 ]; then
         for t in $(find "$build" -type f -name 'tst_*' -perm -u+x | sort); do
+            case " ${SKIP:-} " in *" $(basename "$t") "*)
+                echo "--- $(basename "$t") not run: $SKIP_WHY" >> "$log"
+                continue;;
+            esac
             count=$((count + 1))
             echo "--- $(basename "$t")" >> "$log"
             # shellcheck disable=SC2086
@@ -117,6 +121,12 @@ for c in "${CHECKS[@]}"; do
         done;;
     tsan)
         for cc in "${COMPILERS[@]}"; do
+            # QtDBus works in a thread of its own inside the system Qt,
+            # which has no TSan instrumentation and hands data over under
+            # futex-based QMutex that TSan cannot see, so it reports Qt's
+            # own message copying. None of voicecall's code runs on that
+            # thread; the D-Bus test still runs under ASan and valgrind.
+            SKIP="tst_dbusservice" SKIP_WHY="QtDBus' own thread is not instrumented" \
             check "tsan-$(cc_name "$cc")" "$cc" "$TSAN_FLAGS" \
                 "setarch $(uname -m) -R $RUNNER" TSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1
         done;;
